// RUN: hls-est %s --bram-analysis --bram-attribute-globals --bram-debug > %t.out 2> %t.err
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.err --check-prefix=DBG
// RUN: hls-est %s --bram-analysis=bram-formula=n6 --bram-attribute-globals | FileCheck %s

// A read-only bank (a constant global, priced as a ROM with
// --bram-attribute-globals) by its read ports per cycle (VITIS_NOTES.md N8 (b),
// (c); Vitis 2025.1 kernels ~/hls-est-work/exp-src/formula/fr_rom{1,2,3,4}r_w32_d512,
// a 512x32 table read 1-4 times per iteration of an II=1 loop):
//   1 read   ROM_1P  one read-only port: SDP, x36             -> 1  (Vitis 1)
//   2 reads  ROM_2P  two read-only ports: SDP, x36            -> 1  (Vitis 1;
//            a RAM read twice per cycle would be 2)
//   3 reads  ROM_NP  ceil(3/2) = 2 dual-port ROMs at x18, 2 each -> 4 (Vitis 4)
//   4 reads  ROM_NP  ceil(4/2) = 2 ROMs                       -> 4  (Vitis 4)
// (not n - 1 replicas: 3 reads would be 2 x 2 = 4 as well, 4 reads 3 x 2 = 6.)
// W7 (N26): a ROM is priced at the width its values need, so the table's first
// word is the 32-bit 0x9adf1b1e of the Vitis kernels' tables (random 32-bit
// words), which keeps it a 32-bit table as in those kernels.
// The same under bram-formula=n6 (512 words: the two formulas agree).
// Hand-written lowered IR (II 1, all reads in one stage): the scheduler of
// --convert-affine-to-loopschedule offers a global only two port slots per
// cycle today, so from affine input a ROM read 3 or 4 times per iteration gets
// II 2 and 2 reads per cycle (ROM_2P, 1) where Vitis keeps II 1 and spends 4
// (OPEN_ISSUES.md O26).

// CHECK: kind=ROM_1P  bram=1
// CHECK: kind=ROM_2P  bram=1
// CHECK: kind=ROM_NP  bram=4
// CHECK: kind=ROM_NP  bram=4
// CHECK: Total BRAM: 10

// DBG: ram type: ROM_1P -- {{.*}}peak 1 read(s) per cycle
// DBG: bank math: {{.*}} -> 1 block(s); formula band: depth <= 512, SDP: ceil(W/36)
// DBG: ram type: ROM_2P -- {{.*}}peak 2 read(s) per cycle
// DBG: bank math: {{.*}} -> 1 block(s); formula band: depth <= 512, SDP: ceil(W/36)
// The per-loop line follows the ROM_NP model too (ceil(need/2), not need - 1).
// DBG: 3R+0W per iteration -> ceil(3/1)=3 port-cycles -> copies 2
// DBG: ram type: ROM_NP -- {{.*}}peak 3 read(s) per cycle -> ROM_NP, 2 copies = ceil(n/2) at x18
// DBG: bank math: {{.*}} -> 2 per copy, replication 2 -> 4 block(s); formula band: depth <= 512, not SDP: ceil(W/18)
// DBG: 4R+0W per iteration -> ceil(4/1)=4 port-cycles -> copies 2
// DBG: ram type: ROM_NP -- {{.*}}peak 4 read(s) per cycle -> ROM_NP, 2 copies = ceil(n/2) at x18
// DBG: bank math: {{.*}} -> 2 per copy, replication 2 -> 4 block(s); formula band: depth <= 512, not SDP: ceil(W/18)

module {
